      "passage": "POLICY UPDATE MEMORANDUM\nTo: All Global Employees\nFrom: Corporate Finance & Accounting Department\nDate: January 15\nSubject: Updated Global Travel & Entertainment Expense Policy (Policy #FN-202)\n\nEffective February 1, the following revisions to our Global Travel & Entertainment Policy will apply to all business-related travel booked by company employees.\n\n1. Flight Class Eligibility:\n• Domestic Flights (under 5 hours continuous flight time): All personnel must book Standard Economy class.\n• Transcontinental & International Flights (exceeding 6 hours continuous flight time): Employees are authorized to book Premium Economy. Vice Presidents and Executive Directors are eligible for Business Class.\n\n2. Lodging Caps:\nNightly hotel reimbursement limits have been adjusted to reflect regional cost variations: Major Metros (New York, London, Tokyo, San Francisco): up to $280/night; Tier-2 Cities: up to $190/night. Any exception exceeding these limits by more than 15% requires prior written approval from the departmental Vice President.\n\n3. Meal Per Diem:\nA daily meal allowance of $85.00 is provided ($20 breakfast, $25 lunch, $40 dinner). Itemized receipts are required for all individual expenses exceeding $25.00; credit card summary slips without itemization will not be accepted.",
