      "passage": "INTERNATIONAL TRADE & CUSTOMS COMPLIANCE ADVISORY\nIssued By: Global Trade Advisory Practice | Morrison & Sterling LLP\nDate: May 12 | Advisory Ref: TC-2026-05\nSubject: Updated Harmonized Tariff Schedule (HTS) Classifications for Advanced Semiconductor Equipment\n\nExecutive Summary:\nThe Department of Commerce's Bureau of Industry and Security (BIS), in coordination with international export control regimes, has finalized revisions to tariff classifications and licensing requirements for high-numerical-aperture extreme ultraviolet (EUV) lithography systems and advanced atomic layer deposition (ALD) equipment.\n\nKey Compliance Implications for Importers and Exporters:\n1. Harmonized Tariff Schedule Reclassifications: Effective June 1, specific multi-beam electron pattern generators previously classified under generic sub-heading HTS 8486.20 will be assigned dedicated sub-heading HTS 8486.20.95, carrying an adjusted ad valorem tariff rate of 4.5%.\n2. Validated End-User (VEU) Exemptions: Shipments dispatched to overseas semiconductor fabrication facilities holding active VEU status remain eligible for expedited export licensing; however, quarterly post-shipment verification audits will now be mandatory.\n3. Documentation Deadlines: Freight forwarders must ensure all electronic export information (EEI) filings in the Automated Commercial Environment (ACE) reflect the new 10-digit tariff codes beginning at 00:01 EST on June 1 to prevent border customs holds.",
