      "passage": "FEDERAL AVIATION REGULATORY COMPLIANCE BULLETIN\nAirworthiness Directive Reference: AD-2027-04-19\nTarget Audience: Certified Part 145 Repair Stations, Fleet Maintenance Directors\nSubject: Mandatory Ultrasonic Inspection of Auxiliary Hydraulic Pump Flange Seals\nEffective Date: Immediately upon receipt\n\nApplicability:\nThis directive applies to all commercial transport aircraft equipped with AeroHydraulic Model HP-900 series auxiliary hydraulic power units with over 3,500 flight operating hours.\n\nBackground:\nRecent fleet telemetry data and two uncontained pressure loss incidents have identified fatigue-induced micro-fissures in the titanium retaining flange seals of HP-900 units. If unaddressed, this condition can lead to rapid hydraulic fluid depletion during thrust reverser deployment upon landing.\n\nRequired Actions:\n1. Initial Inspection: Conduct non-destructive ultrasonic and eddy-current inspections of hydraulic flange retaining bolts within 150 flight cycles or 30 calendar days, whichever occurs first.\n2. Replacement Criteria: Flanges exhibiting micro-fractures exceeding 0.05 mm in depth must be removed from service immediately and replaced with reinforced titanium alloy assemblies (Part #HP-900-REV-C).\n3. Record Keeping: Document all inspection results in the aircraft permanent airframe logbook and transmit compliance confirmation forms to the FAA Regional Flight Standards Division within 48 hours of inspection completion.\n\nNon-compliance with this directive renders the affected aircraft unairworthy for commercial passenger operations.",
