      "passage": "THE CRESTVIEW LUXURY HOTEL GROUP\nEMPLOYEE HANDBOOK EXCERPT: SECTION 7 – GUEST PRIVACY & CONCIERGE INTEGRITY\n\n7.1 Confidentiality of High-Profile Guests\nThe Crestview reputation hinges upon discreet, flawless hospitality. Employees are strictly prohibited from disclosing the presence, identity, room numbers, travel schedules, dining habits, or security arrangements of any registered guest, including dignitaries, corporate executives, and entertainment figures.\n• Photography and Video: Staff may not photograph guests or their accompanying entourages anywhere on property.\n• Social Media: Under no circumstances may staff post comments, pictures, or hints regarding guest visits on personal social media platforms. Violation of this clause constitutes gross misconduct resulting in immediate termination and potential civil liability.\n\n7.2 Gratuity and Gift Acceptance Guidelines\nWhile nominal monetary tips for personalized concierge or bell staff service are customary and permissible, employees must decline any non-monetary gifts (including luxury merchandise, event tickets, or vouchers) valued in excess of $150. Any unsolicited gift exceeding this threshold must be reported to the Hotel Ethics Officer within 24 hours for logging or charitable donation.",
