      "passage": "NETLINK FIBER ENTERPRISE NETWORKS\nINCIDENT POST-MORTEM REPORT & SERVICE LEVEL ADVISORY\nIncident Ticket Ref: INC-2027-08832 | Priority: P1 (Critical Outage)\nTo: Enterprise Dedicated Internet Access (DIA) Clients (Seattle Metro Area)\nDate: August 24\n\nIncident Overview:\nOn Thursday, August 23, at approximately 09:14 PST, a major third-party construction excavation contractor severed a 288-strand high-density fiber-optic backbone cable along the Highway 99 transit corridor. This fiber cut affected primary and secondary redundant circuits serving enterprise clients in downtown Seattle and Bellevue.\n\nResolution Timeline:\n• 09:18 PST: NetLink automated network monitoring detected optical carrier loss; emergency response crews dispatched.\n• 10:35 PST: Fiber splicing engineers arrived on site and established a safe excavation perimeter.\n• 13:45 PST: Splicing of all 288 core strands completed; carrier wave restoration confirmed across all 14 nodes.\n• 14:10 PST: Full network latency returned to baseline (<3.2 ms); ticket closed. Total outage duration: 4 hours 56 minutes.\n\nSLA Credit Claims:\nUnder Section 5.2 of the NetLink Master Service Agreement, impacted enterprise clients are entitled to a 15% monthly billing credit for outages exceeding four hours. To claim your credit, submit your account ID to sla-claims@netlinkfiber.com before September 15.",
