      "passage": "SOLARIA EPC INFRASTRUCTURE GROUP\nCERTIFICATE OF SUBSTANTIAL COMPLETION & GRID SYNCHRONIZATION\nProject: Solaria Helios Phase IV Photovoltaic Power Plant (120 MWac)\nLocation: Mojave County, CA | Owner: Solaria Green Infrastructure Fund\nEPC Contractor: Pacific Industrial Builders Inc. (PIB)\nDate of Issuance: August 15\n\nPacific Industrial Builders Inc. hereby certifies that the engineering, procurement, and construction (EPC) works for Helios Phase IV have attained Substantial Completion as of August 14.\n\nKey Milestone Achievements:\n1. Equipment Installation: 280,000 bifacial monocrystalline silicon solar modules, 24 central inverters, and 12 medium-voltage transformer stations have been fully installed and tested.\n2. Substation Grid Synchronization: Interconnection with the regional 230 kV high-voltage transmission grid was energized and synchronized without incident at 11:20 AM on August 14.\n3. 72-Hour Continuous Reliability Test: The plant achieved an average Performance Ratio (PR) of 83.4% during the mandatory 72-hour commissioning test run, surpassing the contractual guaranteed threshold of 81.0%.\n4. Warranty & Punch List: The two-year comprehensive EPC warranty period takes effect starting August 15. Minor civil punch list items (such as perimeter gravel regrading) must be resolved within 30 days.",
