      "passage": "PACIFIC MARITIME FREIGHT ASSOCIATION\nADVISORY NOTICE: EMERGENCY PEAK SEASON CONGESTION SURCHARGE (PCS)\nEffective Date: November 1\nApplicability: All Eastbound Transpacific Ocean Cargo discharging at Ports of Los Angeles and Long Beach\n\nDue to severe vessel berthing delays, acute railhead chassis shortages, and extended terminal dwell times currently exceeding an average of 9.4 days at Southern California marine terminals, member ocean carriers will implement an Emergency Peak Season Congestion Surcharge (PCS).\n\nTerms & Fee Structure:\n1. Surcharge Amount: A standard rate of $650 per 20-foot standard container (TEU) and $1,100 per 40-foot standard or high-cube container (FEU) will be assessed on all laden containerized import shipments.\n2. Exemption Criteria: Cargo routed under intermodal through-bills of lading (IPI/MLB) destined for inland rail ramps outside California, Arizona, and Nevada shall be exempt from this surcharge, provided that rail interchange billing is confirmed prior to vessel arrival.\n3. Billing Procedure: The PCS will be invoiced directly to the consignee listed on the ocean bill of lading and must be settled in full prior to cargo release at the marine terminal gate.\n\nQuestions regarding specific consignment billing should be directed to the Carrier Documentation Portal.",
