      "passage": "CUSTOMS & BORDER PROTECTION TARIFF DISPUTE TRIBUNAL\nOFFICIAL RULING ON HARMONIZED TARIFF SCHEDULE (HTS) CLASSIFICATION\nCase Reference: CBP-REV-2026-094\nImporter: Apex Cross-Border Logistics LLC\nGoods: Wearable Smart Fitness Trackers with Heart-Rate Monitoring and Optical Glucose Sensor\n\nBackground:\nApex Cross-Border Logistics filed a formal appeal challenging the reassessment of import duties on Entry #782-990142. The port authority had reclassified the imported devices under HTS Code 9031.80.80 (Measuring and checking optical instruments, dutiable at 3.5%) rather than the declared HTS Code 8517.62.00 (Machines for the transmission or reception of voice, data, or other information, duty-free).\n\nTribunal Finding:\nUpon technical disassembly and functional evaluation of the device circuitry, the Tribunal determined that the principal essential character of the merchandise is wireless Bluetooth data synchronization with mobile smartphones. The biometric optical sensors serve as auxiliary data input components rather than standalone diagnostic measuring apparatus.\n\nOrder & Disposition:\n1. The tariff classification under HTS Code 8517.62.00 is hereby reinstated.\n2. The Port of Long Beach is directed to refund excess duties assessed totaling $184,350 to Apex Cross-Border Logistics within 60 days of this decree.\n3. This decision constitutes a final administrative determination binding on all standard shipments of this specific model series.",
