      "passage": "FRESH-MART SUPERMARKET CHAIN\nFACILITY SAFETY PROTOCOL: COMMERCIAL REFRIGERATION LEAK RESPONSE\nDocument: SOP-REF-2026-08\nApplicable Sites: All 84 Fresh-Mart Retail Locations\nEffective: July 1\n\nIn compliance with EPA Section 608 Clean Air Act regulations, all store managers and refrigeration technicians must execute the following procedures upon detection of a commercial refrigerant leak:\n\nImmediate Response Actions:\n1. Audible Alarm Activation: If the fixed infrared refrigerant sensor in the central compressor machine room detects R-448A or CO2 (R-744) concentrations exceeding 25 ppm, an amber strobe and localized audible horn will activate.\n2. Emergency Machine Room Ventilation: Technicians must verify that the automated dual exhaust purge fans have engaged, providing continuous 20 air changes per hour.\n3. Leak Pinpointing & Electronic Sniffing: Certified HVAC technicians equipped with heated diode electronic leak detectors must scan all evaporator coil joints, suction header valves, and braze points.\n4. Mandatory Repair Window: Under federal EPA regulations, any commercial refrigeration system with a charge greater than 50 pounds exhibiting an annualized leak rate exceeding 20% must be fully repaired and verified via pressure decay test within thirty (30) days of leak identification.\n5. Recordkeeping: Log all refrigerant added or recovered in the digital EPA Compliance Dashboard within 24 hours of servicing.",
