      "passage": "LLOYD'S MARITIME UNDERWRITING SYNDICATE 448\n50 Leadenhall Street, London EC3A 2AQ, United Kingdom\n\nMEMORANDUM OF COMPLIANCE & SURVEY REQUIREMENT\nDate: May 12\nTo: Ocean Crest Shipping Ltd. (Attn: Fleet Technical Director)\nRegarding: Hull & Machinery Insurance Policy #HM-2024-99120\nVessel: MV Polaris Vanguard (IMO 9481024 / Bulk Carrier / 82,000 DWT)\n\nDear Technical Director,\n\nOur marine risk assessment records indicate that the MV Polaris Vanguard is approaching the statutory expiration of its 5-year Special Hull Survey cycle on August 31.\n\nTo maintain continuous, uninterrupted Hull & Machinery insurance coverage without policy conditional warranties or deductible adjustments, Ocean Crest Shipping Ltd. must arrange for an accredited IACS classification society surveyor to perform a full underwater hull inspection and ultrasonic steel plate thickness measurement at an approved drydock facility prior to the expiration date.\n\nA certified copy of the surveyor's intermediate condition report, confirming that bottom hull plating corrosion wastage does not exceed 10% of original nominal thickness, must be submitted to our underwriting team no later than September 15.\n\nFailure to provide documented proof of drydock completion by the deadline will result in immediate suspension of policy coverage for hull damage and grounding risks.\n\nSincerely,\nArthur Pendelton\nSenior Marine Underwriting Officer",
