      "passage": "PARSONS INFRASTRUCTURE ENGINEERING CONSULTANTS\nSTRUCTURAL HEALTH MONITORING SUMMARY REPORT\nTo: State Department of Transportation (Bridge Maintenance Division)\nProject: Golden Reach Cable-Stayed Bridge (Structure No. BR-4019)\nInspection Date: July 8 | Report ID: SHM-2026-88\n\n1. Scope of Investigation:\nParsons Infrastructure conducted non-destructive ultrasonic guided-wave testing (UGWT) and magnetic flux leakage (MFL) scanning on all sixty-four (64) parallel wire stay cables supporting the main 1,200-meter navigation span.\n\n2. Key Inspection Findings:\n• Cables S-01 through S-13 & S-15 through S-64: Exhibited nominal tensile stress distribution and sound high-density polyethylene (HDPE) outer sheathing with no structural wire fractures.\n• Cable S-14 (South Tower, Lower Stay Anchor): Ultrasonic telemetry identified localized internal corrosion wastage of approximately 4.2% metallic cross-sectional area near the lower guide tube anchor socket, caused by degraded elastomeric neoprene water seals.\n\n3. Mandatory Recommendations:\n• Immediate Sealant Remediation: Maintenance crews must inject zinc-rich anti-corrosion polyurethane sealant into the lower anchorage socket of Cable S-14 within sixty (60) calendar days to halt moisture ingress.\n• Re-Inspection Interval: Perform a follow-up ultrasonic stress evaluation on Cable S-14 in six (6) months.",
