      "passage": "TÜV RHEINLAND CERTIFICATION SERVICES (EU NOTIFIED BODY 0197)\nMEDICAL DEVICE REGULATION (EU MDR 2017/745) AUDIT REPORT\nManufacturer: BioPulse Cardiovascular Instruments Ltd.\nDevice: UltraFlow™ Drug-Eluting Coronary Stent System (Class III)\nAudit Type: Stage 2 Technical Documentation & Post-Market Surveillance Review\nLead Auditor: Dr. Heinrich Müller | Date: September 24\n\nAudit Findings Summary:\nThe technical documentation for the UltraFlow™ Drug-Eluting Coronary Stent System was evaluated for conformity with Annex IX of EU Regulation 2017/745. The audit revealed one (1) Major Non-Conformity (MNC) and two (2) Minor Non-Conformities.\n\nMajor Non-Conformity (MNC-01): Clinical Evaluation & PMCF\nThe Post-Market Clinical Follow-up (PMCF) plan lacks statistically powered long-term (5-year) registry data regarding late stent thrombosis in diabetic patient cohorts. The current clinical evaluation report relies disproportionately on literature equivalence data from predicate first-generation bare-metal stents rather than head-to-head clinical trial data for the paclitaxel polymer coating.\n\nCorrective Action Requirement:\nBioPulse must submit a formal Root Cause Analysis (RCA) and a revised PMCF clinical registry protocol within sixty (60) calendar days. Failure to resolve MNC-01 prior to December 15 will result in the suspension of the CE Mark Conformity Certificate.",
